Z||000000||rogergarrison||07-09-2001||08:01 PM||||Ok, I broke one of my front turn signal lenses on my Ferrari kit. Dont ask. Called Rodney to see if he had any replacement. He didnt and neither did any Ferrari dealer I could find in US. Rodney gave me a number to try and strange it was in my area code. He had the lenses in stock for both sides for only $45 each. (Ferrari wanted $169 each and couldnt even get them). So this guy is only like 20 minute drive from my house so he gave me directions and I told him I was on the way. Found this really nice pole building out in the boondocks. went inside and stood jaw agape. this room is stacked to the ceiling with tons and tons of Ferrari stuff. Dozens of complete engines from Dina V6's to Boxer 512 turbocharged 12 cyls. Transaxles, wheels, you name it. He admired my car and finally figured out it was a kit. then he took me to the other building behind it. There is a whole garage full of cars under covers. A F-1 ready to run, a l967 coupe for $350,000,a Daytona coupe,several Testa Rossas, 328 GTBs, GTB-4,TR's, 2 Mangustas, 3 race ready Lancia Stratos. He wanted to know if id be interested in painting one of them for vintage racing. Hed just got it back from Italy where the frame and body had just been totally rebuilt to new. I didnt even get to see everything in there. I want this guy for a neighbor.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. I dont even  know how many millions of dollars of stuff is there. I know the engines start at $25,000 and I saw at least 30 ready to run, not including ones in crates. I didnt get anything done in my shop, spent the whole afternoon in heaven. Oh yes and MANY THANKS RODNEY. (Rodney comes thru again, he could have sold me a new complete set for $200 but passed me on to a better buy giving away a sale). <P>sorry about the long post, but I was just amazed that this was hiding out in a field all this time.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781">  <p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 07-10-2001).]||||reg||10
